    "rich_text_4G647V": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_EwKxL3": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Additional Training and Integrative Approaches",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text_color": "",
            "gradient": ""
          }
        },
        "richtext_TadjHP": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "paragraph_class_name": "richtext-p-section",
            "content": "<p></p><p><strong>Internal Family Systems (IFS)</strong><br/>Facilitates understanding of internal emotional systems and supports more organized, compassionate engagement with those parts.</p><p><strong>Emotional Freedom Technique (EFT)</strong><br/>Adjunctive tapping-based approach used to support emotional regulation and reduction of distress.</p><p><strong>Trauma-Conscious Yoga (TCY)</strong><br/>Incorporates trauma-sensitive, body-based practices to support regulation and reconnection.</p><p><strong>Somatic Psychology (SP)</strong><br/>Integrates mind-body awareness into treatment, with attention to nervous system functioning and embodied experience.</p><p><strong>Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction </strong></p><p>Training in Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction has informed Dr. Serravalle’s work in helping clients develop greater awareness of internal experience, reduce reactivity, and build more intentional responses to stress. This background supports treatment that emphasizes attention, self-observation, nervous system regulation, and the cultivation of skills that promote resilience and emotional balance.</p><p><strong>Breathwork</strong><br/>Uses structured breathing techniques to support grounding, regulation, and emotional awareness in context of healing and growth.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
